---
/* L60 - raw calls, a run record, a derived report. One writer: the figures workstream C. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L60.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of an open ledger on a desk whose entries are each marked with a small clock, a cable running from the book to a printed chart of four rising bars, with a pencil, a glass of water and a stack of blank sheets nearby."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L60-fig-title L60-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L60-fig-title">The raw calls, the run record, and the report derived from them</title>
      <desc id="L60-fig-desc">
        Three panels left to right. The first holds a stack of short horizontal strokes under a title naming a jsonl file, with a note that it is one line per call in order. The second, a smaller panel, holds a run record with a jagged fingerprint line and a note about the question set. The third, tinted, is the report, with three bars and a label saying it is derived and never hand-edited. An arrow curves from the raw panel over the top into the report, labelled derived from the raw calls, and a shorter arrow leads from the run record into the report. The panels rise into place and the arrows draw themselves after.
      </desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="L60-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="var(--color-ink-45)" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <rect class="m-rise" style="--m-duration: 0.6s;" x="40" y="86" width="160" height="160" fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="54" y="110" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink)">runs/&lt;id&gt;.jsonl</text>
      <line x1="54" y1="122" x2="186" y2="122" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="54" y1="140" x2="160" y2="140" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="54" y1="154" x2="176" y2="154" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="54" y1="168" x2="140" y2="168" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="54" y1="182" x2="170" y2="182" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="54" y1="196" x2="128" y2="196" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="54" y1="210" x2="164" y2="210" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="54" y1="224" x2="146" y2="224" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="54" y="272" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">one line per call, in order</text>

      <rect class="m-rise" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 0.3s;" x="240" y="116" width="140" height="100" fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="254" y="140" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink)">&lt;id&gt;.meta.json</text>
      <line x1="254" y1="152" x2="366" y2="152" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <path d="M 254 172 L 266 172 L 272 164 L 280 180 L 288 168 L 296 176 L 306 166 L 316 174 L 326 168 L 340 174" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="254" y="200" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">run label, price, cases</text>
      <text x="254" y="246" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">a fingerprint of the question set</text>

      <rect class="m-rise" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 0.6s;" x="420" y="86" width="170" height="160" fill="var(--color-prussian-tint)" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="434" y="110" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-prussian)">&lt;id&gt;.md</text>
      <line x1="434" y1="122" x2="576" y2="122" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <rect x="440" y="204" width="24" height="30" fill="var(--color-prussian)" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <rect x="474" y="184" width="24" height="50" fill="var(--color-prussian)" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <rect x="508" y="148" width="24" height="86" fill="var(--color-prussian)" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="434" y="272" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-prussian)">derived, never hand-edited</text>

      <path class="m-draw" style="--m-length: 321; --m-duration: 1.2s; --m-delay: 0.8s;" d="M 200 70 L 505 70 L 505 82" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L60-arrow)" />
      <text x="330" y="62" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">derived from the raw calls</text>
      <path class="m-draw" style="--m-length: 110; --m-duration: 1s; --m-delay: 1s;" d="M 380 166 L 416 166" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L60-arrow)" />

      <text x="40" y="312" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">a number with no raw notes behind it is marketing</text>

    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L60</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">The raw calls are kept in order, the run record sits beside them, and the readable summary is only ever derived from those two - never typed by hand.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  /* scoped to this figure */
  .fig__svg {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
